  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If <math><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is&nbsp;the amplitude of the electric field then the intensity of the electromagnetic wave is given as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>c</mi></math>. From the above relation, we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>. The relation between electric and magnetic fields is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></math>. The direction&nbsp;of <math> <mrow> <mover accent=\"true\"> <mi>E</mi> <mo stretchy=\"true\">&#8594;</mo> </mover> <mo>&#215;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"> <mi>B</mi> <mo stretchy=\"true\">&#8594;</mo> </mover> </mrow> </math> will be along <math><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math>.",
